# Scathach

## Lore

The Scathach (pronounced scah thach) take their name from a Celtic warrior goddess, Scathach nUanaind, heralded for her martial arts, combat skills and physical prowess. These woodland druids are both warriors and blacksmiths, expert metal- and wood-workers who make and use magic stones, iron and wood. Their herb magic serves their forge: magic cauldrons, irons and weapons, and items of protection.

## GM Notes

A magic cauldron takes months to make, in three stages each worked at a place of magic during a time of peak energy. Like the other druids, the Scathach are careful not to make too many magic items and not to give or sell them to people who will misuse them. Traditional garb is a shirt and pants of any color, black insulated boots, gloves and a black work apron; most wear heavy armor on the road. Starting kit beyond the sheet: three dozen large nails.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'scathach');


